//@ compile-fail
//@ requires: madaros
//@ error-pattern: E035
//@ sabotage: SOUNIO_EFFECT_INFER
//
// An INFERRED effect must cross a module boundary. Measured 2026-08-21: it did
// not, and the failure was silent -- rc=0, no diagnostic, the obligation gone.
//
// Isolated with an A/B pair differing in ONE clause in the middle module:
//
//   pub fn mid_calls(x: i64) -> i64 with Panic { deep_panics(x) }
//     -> top += Panic (from mid_calls); main += Panic (from top)   reaches
//   pub fn mid_calls(x: i64) -> i64 { deep_panics(x) }
//     -> mid_calls += Panic (from deep_panics), and stops
//
// Cause: modules are checked in list order, so a caller in an earlier module
// is checked before the body of its callee in a later module has widened that
// callee's row. A DECLARED effect is in the signature table from the collect
// pass and crosses fine; an INFERRED one is added while the callee's body is
// walked, and by then the importer has been and gone.
//
// This is the single-file form of the same shape, which must keep being
// refused with inference OFF: the caller declares nothing and the callee
// declares Panic. The sabotage knob is SOUNIO_EFFECT_INFER because turning
// inference ON is exactly what must make this refusal disappear.

fn leaf(x: i64) -> i64 with Panic {
    if x < 0 { panic("neg") }
    x
}

fn caller_without_panic(x: i64) -> i64 {
    leaf(x)
}

fn main() -> i64 with IO {
    println("unreachable")
    caller_without_panic(1)
}
